P0 foundation, P1/P1.5 commercial surface and P4 machine surfaces for the
search and AI-retrieval work. Full reasoning in
EXECUTION_REPORT_SEARCH_AI_2026-08-24.md.

THE DEPARTURE FROM THE BRIEF

Thirty-four commercial slugs were requested as thirty-four pages. One page was
written; the other thirty-three slugs are permanent redirects into it and into
pages that already existed. A page per slug is a doorway set under Google's
published spam policy, it splits the links and crawl budget one page would
concentrate, and — the part that matters most here — every retrieval system
deduplicates near-identical documents before ranking, so thin variants are one
weak citation target rather than many strong ones. The brief's own goal is
damaged by the tactic the brief asked for. Reasoning is in the header of
content/search/topic-map.ts.

WHAT THE NEW GUARDS FOUND

· 49 NAP literals on customer surfaces, including TWO separate LocalBusiness
  graphs (root-schema.ts site-wide, structured-data.ts on 32 area pages) each
  with its own hand-typed copy of nine identity fields. verify-business-facts
  bans the RETIRED number and cannot ban the current one, so a literal copy of
  today's number passed every guard until the day it changes.
· The three price bands typed by hand in four places — including FAQ_ITEMS,
  which is emitted as FAQPage JSON-LD on every page, and a paper served as PDF.
· The footer printed the city twice in its address.
· Two phone inputs used the company's number as the customer's format hint.
· The RenoGuide prompt hard-coded "est. 2000" and "a 25-year reputation".
· A cluster-intent collision in the new topic map itself, caught by its own
  guard, now recorded as the site's largest content gap rather than relabelled.

Two inconsistencies are registered and reported but NOT edited, because both are
owner decisions: the unsourced 99.7% dust-capture figure (19 places, two inside
FAQPage JSON-LD, with a measured 99.5% in the case studies) and two incompatible
warranty statements. Deadline 2026-10-31, then seo:claims --strict.

VERIFICATION

tsc --noEmit: 107 errors before, 107 after — identical set, all pre-existing and
all caused by prisma generate failing in this environment (403 on the binary
host). Zero new errors across ~60 edits in 40 files. All 27 existing verify:*
scripts pass. next build and the two live checks could not run here and must be
run from the Codespace.

